{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1167","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Range Deleting"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array consisting of $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots , a_n$$$ and an integer $$$x$$$. It is guaranteed that for every $$$i$$$, $$$1 \\le a_i \\le x$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's denote a function $$$f(l, r)$$$ which erases all values such that $$$l \\le a_i \\le r$$$ from the array $$$a$$$ and returns the resulting array. For example, if $$$a = [4, 1, 1, 4, 5, 2, 4, 3]$$$, then $$$f(2, 4) = [1, 1, 5]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to calculate the number of pairs $$$(l, r)$$$ such that $$$1 \\le l \\le r \\le x$$$ and $$$f(l, r)$$$ is sorted in non-descending order. Note that the empty array is also considered sorted."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$x$$$ ($$$1 \\le n, x \\le 10^6$$$) — the length of array $$$a$$$ and the upper limit for its elements, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le x$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the number of pairs $$$1 \\le l \\le r \\le x$$$ such that $$$f(l, r)$$$ is sorted in non-descending order."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 3\n2 3 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7 4\n1 3 1 2 2 4 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case correct pairs are $$$(1, 1)$$$, $$$(1, 2)$$$, $$$(1, 3)$$$ and $$$(2, 3)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case correct pairs are $$$(1, 3)$$$, $$$(1, 4)$$$, $$$(2, 3)$$$, $$$(2, 4)$$$, $$$(3, 3)$$$ and $$$(3, 4)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1167E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1167/problem/E"}